    "contract_text": "Write the reader-facing manuscript in natural, idiomatic Korean (spelling: ko-KR). Compose directly in Korean — do not write in another language and translate, and do not imitate foreign grammar or idioms. Use standard Korean punctuation (double quotation marks for dialogue, the ellipsis character) and natural Korean sentences with proper spacing and particles. Render address terms, titles, and speech levels the way Korean speakers of this setting would actually speak them — the speech-level and honorific system is part of the prose, used correctly and naturally, never as a romanized suffix attached to a name. Use only the approved terms listed in the terminology notes. Do not produce translation-like Korean and do not drift into literary or Western-novel diction.",
    "punctuation": {
      "dialogue_quotes": "“ ”",
      "nested_quotes": "‘ ’",
      "thought_style": "plain",
      "dash": "em_unspaced",
      "ellipsis": "…"
    },
